.TH ACTIVE-RPC-CLI 1 "2026-10-31" "active-rpc-cli 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
active-rpc-cli \- capability-based RPC peer, caller and load generator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B active-rpc-cli
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B active-rpc-cli
drives the real Active RPC capability kernel and transport stack. Peers mint
capabilities, calls travel as native ARP1 envelopes, and refusals surface their
stable
.I rpc/...
codes. Interop transports (Connect, HTTP/2) are adapters; native ARP1 over TCP
is the baseline.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B doctor
Version, transports, compiled features, budget defaults and exit codes.
.TP
.B peer [--transport tcp|http2|connect|quic] [--limit N] [--methods echo,sum] [--cert-out PATH]
Start a demo peer with a real kernel and one minted capability. Prints
transport, addr, cap and, for
.BR quic ,
the certificate path.
.B --limit
counts connections for tcp and http2, requests for connect and calls for quic.
.TP
.B call --addr \fIHOST:PORT\fR [--transport ...] [--cap HEX] [--method M] [--payload FILE | --text TEXT] [--cert FILE]
Issue one call and print kind, id, payload length and the decoded value.
.TP
.B pipeline --addr \fIHOST:PORT\fR --cap \fIHEX\fR [--calls N] [--method M] [--payload FILE]
Send N calls on one connection before reading any response; prints the
round-trip count.
.TP
.B loadgen --addr \fIHOST:PORT\fR --cap \fIHEX\fR [--requests N] [--concurrency C] [--method M] [--payload FILE]
Controlled load over C connections; prints p50, p95, p99 and throughput.
.TP
.B bridge [--limit N]
Serve the Connect/gRPC interop adapter against the demo kernel.
.TP
.B events [--plane URL] [--after ID] [--follow] [--interval-ms N]
Tail the control-plane event stream. Events carry correlation ids, never raw
authority.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Refusal or a failed request, for example
.I rpc/method-not-granted
or
.IR rpc/unknown-capability .
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.TP
.B 3
Transport or codec failure: connect, handshake or frame.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
active-rpc-cli peer --limit 4 > peer.txt
ADDR=$(awk -F= '/^addr=/{print $2}' peer.txt)
CAP=$(awk -F= '/^cap=/{print $2}' peer.txt)
active-rpc-cli call --addr "$ADDR" --cap "$CAP" --method echo --text hello
active-rpc-cli pipeline --addr "$ADDR" --cap "$CAP" --calls 16
active-rpc-cli loadgen --addr "$ADDR" --cap "$CAP" --requests 200 --concurrency 8
active-rpc-cli events --plane http://127.0.0.1:8787 --follow
fi
.SH NOTES
Capabilities print as opaque ids; the CLI never prints authority bits or secret
material. The quic peer uses the self-signed demo mode and exits after
.B --limit
calls; the library's own QUIC tests cover mutual TLS and identity binding.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR active-infinity-cli (1)
